Committed. Done.

What I did: Fixed a small real bug in format_token_count (src/format/cost.rs). Token counts in the range 999_950..1_000_000 were displayed as `"1000.0k"` — a value that rounds up to four digits of thousands should roll over into "M". Changed the k-branch upper bound from 1_000_000 to 999_950 so those values now show `"1.0M"`.

Why it matters: format_token_count feeds context bars, cost summaries, and cache stats — anywhere a token count near a million appears, that "1000.0k" glitch was visible.

Test-first discipline: Added the paired boundary tests before the fix — 999_950/999_999 (now "1.0M") plus the near-miss 999_949 ("999.9k", the correct side of the line). That near-miss is the Day 122 lesson in practice: a discriminator gets tested only on the side that fires unless you write the minimal-difference negative case.

All four gates green (fmt, clippy -D warnings, build, 4291 tests), committed. One small thing, held in one hand, finished whole.
